From: umeko build fix <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: fix Makefile corrupted by pasted dtsi fragment

The cancro-klipper tree (bzy-080408/linux-msm8974 @ 24b3f61) has a
commented-out &pm8941_gpios dtsi fragment accidentally pasted into
arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile, fused with the fairphone dtb entry.
make fails with "missing separator" at line 54. Drop the garbage lines
and restore the fairphone entry.

Should be dropped once the submodule is fixed upstream.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile | 11 +----------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
index 87e4e3e..ce4b766 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
@@ -48,16 +48,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM) += \
 	qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-honami.dtb \
 	qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-rhine-togari.dtb \
 	qcom-msm8974-sony-xperia-sirius.dtb \
-
-
-
-//&pm8941_gpios {
-//	gpio_keys_default: gpio-keys-active-state {
-//		pins = "gpio2", "gpio5";
-//		function = "normal";
-//		input-enable;
-//		bias-disable;
-//		power-source 	qcom-msm8974pro-fairphone-fp2.dtb \
+	qcom-msm8974pro-fairphone-fp2.dtb \
 	qcom-msm8974pro-htc-m8.dtb \
 	qcom-msm8974pro-oneplus-bacon.dtb \
 	qcom-msm8974pro-samsung-klte.dtb \
